    {
      "ts": 1790896619.021204,
      "status": "done",
      "result": {
        "summary": "I could not read the T-1520 fix-round diff. The branch no longer exists and the diff was truncated, so I reviewed the base commit fb164d3 and the visible hunks. The gate was green on the first attempt. The four acceptance-named tests exist as unittest methods, and the source behaviour matches the spec: grace turns, nag-once record, default threshold, `--session-id` forwarding. The comments below are non-blocking.",
        "verdict": "approve",
        "comments": [
          {
            "path": "orchestrator/planner_context.py",
            "line": 19,
            "issue": "`session_id` goes straight into a path (`directory / f\"{session_id}.jsonl\"`) and into the printed shell command (`--session-id {session_id}`). A value with `../` or shell metacharacters could read another jsonl file or inject text into the instruction the Planner is told to run. Validate it against `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$` in `_transcript_path` and the hook.",
            "severity": "med"
          },
          {
            "path": "orchestrator/handover.py",
            "line": 285,
            "issue": "`_save_handover_session` runs before the plan.md section is written. If the later write fails, the hook still prints 'handover written' and the Planner is not nagged again. A manual `handover` call without `--session-id` also overwrites another session's record with `session_id: None`, which loses the nag-once state. Write the record after plan.md succeeds, and skip it when `session_id` is None.",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          {
            "path": "orchestrator/cli.py",
            "line": 623,
            "issue": "`tokens_at` is only measured when `--session-id` is given. Otherwise it is None, and the short line can never apply, so the nag-once record has no effect for that call. This is fine as designed, but `ho.add_argument(\"--session-id\")` is undocumented.",
            "severity": "low"
          }
        ],
        "packet_version": "70a7a714ccc0",
        "confidence": 0.0,
        "provenance": [
          "repo"
        ]
      }
    },
